1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,140
Whether it’s studying for exams, working on a project or struggling with a dissertation, we’ve all been under immense stress at some point.
不管是备考、做项目还是绞尽脑汁写论文，我们每个人都有过承受巨大压力的时刻。

2
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:20,880
When it gets a bit overwhelming, we can reach a level of exhaustion that is unprecedented – the dreaded burnout.
当压力大到让人难以承受时，我们会陷入一种前所未有的疲惫状态——也就是令人闻之色变的职业倦怠。

3
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:28,730
However, that feeling of exhaustion is not just physical; it can be mental as well.
但这种疲惫感不只是身体上的，也可能是精神层面的。

4
00:00:28,730 --> 00:00:40,900
According to ‘Psychology Today’, burnout isn’t just caused by working long hours; it is more about prolonged or repeated exposure to a stressful situation.
据《今日心理学》杂志称，职业倦怠的成因不只是长时间工作，更多是源于长期或反复置身于充满压力的环境中。

5
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:46,850
The result can be feelings of cynicism, depression and lethargy.
其后果可能是产生愤世嫉俗、抑郁消沉和无精打采的情绪。

6
00:00:46,850 --> 00:00:56,270
A feeling of loss of control in a work scenario can create a conflict with the sense of self – which can lead to burnout.
在工作场景中失去掌控感，会让人的自我认知产生矛盾，进而引发职业倦怠。

7
00:00:56,270 --> 00:01:01,400
Suffering from burnout can stifle our creativity and productivity.
陷入职业倦怠的状态会扼杀我们的创造力和工作效率。

8
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:08,620
Ironically, this means that striving to be more efficient can result in a reduction in our productivity.
颇具讽刺意味的是，这意味着越是拼命追求高效，反而越会导致效率下降。

9
00:01:08,620 --> 00:01:13,140
But what can we do to avoid the evils of burnout?
那么，我们该如何避免职业倦怠的危害呢？

10
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:16,990
Well, there are some tips that may help you.
其实有一些小技巧可以帮到你。

11
00:01:16,990 --> 00:01:28,450
Psychologist Albert Bandura’s idea of self-efficacy – which is the theory that you should believe in your ability to complete a task at hand - may assist you.
心理学家阿尔伯特·班杜拉提出的自我效能感理论或许能帮到你，该理论的核心是，你要相信自己有能力完成手头的任务。

12
00:01:28,450 --> 00:01:38,290
A feeling that the task is achievable and that you are capable of succeeding means that a difficult task might be less gruelling.
当你觉得任务是可以完成的，并且自己有能力成功时，再棘手的任务也会变得没那么费力。

13
00:01:38,290 --> 00:01:43,340
Finding ways to express your creative side may help.
找到释放创造力的途径也会有所帮助。

14
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:51,270
Not everyone has creative aspects to their jobs, and, therefore, they need to find other outlets.
并非所有人的工作都带有创造性，因此他们需要寻找其他的宣泄渠道。

15
00:01:51,270 --> 00:01:56,170
They could paint, write or take part in local theatre.
比如画画、写作，或是参与当地的戏剧表演。

16
00:01:56,170 --> 00:02:04,410
All of this may help to detach them from the overwhelming stress that may exist in their working life.
这些活动都能帮助人们暂时摆脱工作中难以承受的压力。

17
00:02:04,410 --> 00:02:10,200
Looking after yourself and your surroundings can also be beneficial.
照顾好自己和身处的环境同样有益。

18
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:15,850
The consequence is that you are surrounded by a cleaner and more positive environment.
这样做的结果是，你会被一个更整洁、更积极的环境所包围。

19
00:02:15,850 --> 00:02:23,300
This, in turn, leads to another tip, which is to have healthy and positive thoughts.
这一点又引出了另一个技巧，那就是保持健康积极的心态。

20
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:27,240
Being negative can be incredibly draining.
消极的心态会让人身心俱疲。

21
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:36,640
Having a positive mental attitude towards everything you do means that you may feel more capable as well.
无论做什么事都抱着积极的心态，也会让你觉得自己更有能力应对挑战。

22
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:43,350
Burnout is a common condition associated with the pressures of the modern world.
职业倦怠是一种与现代社会压力相伴而生的普遍状态。

23
00:02:43,350 --> 00:02:53,320
It’s not just a physical condition; it has psychological effects that can impact heavily on your work and life in general.
它不只是一种身体上的不适，其带来的心理影响还会严重干扰我们的工作和日常生活。

24
00:02:53,320 --> 00:03:01,060
Taking steps to avoid burning out can benefit not just us, but our bosses and families.
采取措施预防职业倦怠，不仅对我们自己有益，也能惠及我们的上司和家人。
